## Module boundaries

- **`app/src/screens/`** — page-level components only; no direct Firestore calls.
- **`app/src/services/`** — sole layer allowed to call Firebase SDK or Cloud Functions; screens must go through services.
- **`app/src/store/`** — global state only; no business logic; delegates to services.
- **`app/src/components/`** — pure UI; receives props; no store imports except via hooks.
- **`functions/src/matching/`** — owns all matching algorithm logic; no other module may replicate similarity scoring.
- **`functions/src/middleware/`** — every HTTP/callable handler must pass through `authenticate` before touching Firestore.
- **`app/src/components/ads/`** — AdMob code is isolated here; never inline ad calls in screens.
- Cross-module imports flow **inward only**: screens → hooks → store → services → firebase.ts.

